  "question": {
    "text": "<p>As shown in the figure, a current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;flowing in an equilateral triangle of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> . The magnetic field at the centroid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> of the triangle is :</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0074_0237aa485421.png\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 160px;\" /></p><p>(Neglect the effect of earth&rsquo;s magnetic field)</p>"
  },
