  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0074_0237aa485421.png\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 160px;\" /></p><p>Perpendicular distance of centroid from any of the sides will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mi>tan</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>Each side will subtend an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;at the centre. Also magnetic field due to all sides will be out of plane of paper, hence total magnetic field can be written as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math></p>"
  }
}